     "finding": "All 101 Table S3 observations and NaCl calibrant readings are bundled. The main diagnostic fits 92 heated/MAP rows; all-row and weighting sensitivity results are separately reported. Exact source weights and mask are unpublished."
    },
    "independent_reproduction": {
     "script": "scripts/reproduce_campbell_2009_buffers.py",
     "report": "docs/literature-reproductions/campbell-2009-buffers.md",
     "results": "docs/data/campbell-2009-reproduction.json",
     "benchmark": "Official Tables S4-S5 differentiated through Equation (6), with 0.02 cm3/mol paired-volume tolerance; independent Debye quadrature checks individual equations.",
     "selection": "All Table S2 rows for FeO; only its 15 explicitly fcc rows for Fe. For Ni/NiO, retain all 92 heated/MAP Table S3 rows (T>295 K); exclude its nine 293-295 K quenched DAC rows from the main diagnostic. This exclusion follows the Section 2.2 stress warning but is an audit choice: the authors do not publish a regression row mask. All 101 rows are retained in the dataset and tested in a sensitivity refit."
    }
